  "$comment": "The signature is cryptographically valid over its covered components, so a verifier that does not enforce the nonce requirement accepts it. The verifier answers 403 with Accept-Signature listing nonce among the required parameters. The profile reports signature failures with HTTP status codes (Web Bot Auth sections 5.3 and 5.4). A 403 carries Accept-Signature naming the components and parameters the profile requires, so the signer can sign again. Conformance grades the status code; the accept_signature object describes the header the verifier sends, and the exact serialization is RFC 9421 section 5.1."
